Nothing asked the owner how a helper's ANSWER worked out — the only ask
debrief fires when nobody answers — so 1692's thank-you could start only if
the owner said so unprompted. A first, real answer (not a decline) now arms
one debrief on the asker's goal, three days later, under its own kind
(migration 228 adds 'answered_ask' to debrief_arms). It goes stale once the
owner has recorded whether it helped.

HELD (D44): the instruction the model reads is NIGHT_QUESTIONS AV.
ANSWER_DEBRIEF_ON = false — nothing is armed until Misho's yes. The day-14
line to the helper comes after.

